# monoid-nerd: the Nerd Fonts build of Monoid, its Mono form, whose icons
# are each one cell wide. The font draws the text, Powerline's separators
# and Nerd Fonts' icons, the Font Logos included, and it sets the character
# cell. The set starts at 12 points, 16 pixels at 96 DPI.
#
# check=U+E0B0 is the Powerline arrow, which every Nerd Fonts build holds,
# so it tells the build from a plain font of a similar name.
#
# The Nerd Fonts build holds the icons itself, so the set adds only color
# emoji after it, and GNU Unifont last, which draws every other character.
# vtium ships this font set, never the fonts. Nerd Fonts lists its Font
# Logos icons with no license grant, so no vtium package carries a Nerd
# Fonts file: you install the build yourself. Without it, Unifont draws the
# text and each icon draws as a hollow box.
#
# Licenses: Monoid is under MIT or the SIL OFL 1.1, at your choice. Nerd
# Fonts' patcher is under MIT, and its icon sets are under their own
# licenses: CC-BY-4.0 for Font Awesome and Codicons, Apache-2.0 for Material
# Design Icons, and none for Font Logos. The layers name their own licenses.
#
# References:
# - ADR-1204 D3: the Nerd Fonts category.

name=monoid-nerd
size=12
license=(MIT OR OFL-1.1) AND OFL-1.1 AND MIT AND Apache-2.0 AND CC-BY-4.0

# Nerd Fonts 3.4.0's Monoid Nerd Font Mono.
source=font:Monoid Nerd Font Mono
version=3.4.0
check=U+E0B0
url=https://github.com/ryanoasis/nerd-fonts/releases/tag/v3.4.0

layer=noto-emoji
layer=unifont
